{"alignments": [{"id": "PSA.61.8.a001", "note": "כן → So.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.001"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.001", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t001"], "target_head": "t001"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a002", "note": "זמר rendered sing praise; unto is supplied to reach the bare direct object and joins the verb (rule 44). Headed on sing, both words writing the lexeme as in 'did work'; heading on praise was the competing reading.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.002"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.002", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t002", "t003", "t004", "t005", "t006"], "target_head": "t004"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a003", "note": "Noun → name.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.003"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.003", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t008"], "target_head": "t008"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a004", "note": "Suffix → thy.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.004"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.004", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t007"], "target_head": "t007"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a005", "note": "ל → for; each morpheme of לעד has its own word, so rule 2 splits.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.005"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.005", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t009"], "target_head": "t009"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a006", "note": "עד 'perpetuity' → ever.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.006"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.006", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t010"], "target_head": "t010"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a007", "note": "Purpose ל recast as finite clause takes the complementizer (rule 52).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.007"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.007", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t011"], "target_head": "t011"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a008", "note": "Infinitive keeps modal and lexical verb; subject pronoun goes to its suffix (rule 18).", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.008"], "source_head": "WLC.PSA.61.8.008", "status": "aligned", "target": ["t013", "t015"], "target_head": "t015"}, {"id": "PSA.61.8.a009", "note": "Suffix on infinitive construct is its subject → I.", "source": ["WLC.PSA.61.8.